## 3. BACKEND PROTOCOL (copy exactly)

**Transport (GET, JSONP first, fetch fallback):**
- Every request = `GET {SCRIPT_URL}?action=<name>&<params>&token=<token>&callback=<cbName>&t=<Date.now()>`; all values `encodeURIComponent`'d; null/undefined → empty string.
- Primary: JSONP by injecting a `<script>` with a unique callback name `_gssCb_<ts>_<rand>` (a separate script tag and callback for **each** request so parallel requests never clash). Timeout **25 s** → `{status:'timeout'}`.
- If the script tag errors → retry once with `fetch(url, {method:'GET', redirect:'follow'})`; strip the `callback(...)` wrapper with a regex if present, then `JSON.parse`.
- Long-running actions (e.g. `photoRecall`) use the fetch path, not JSONP.
- Uploads/POST (photo chunks etc.): `fetch(url, {method:'POST', mode:'no-cors', headers:{'Content-Type':'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'}, body:URLSearchParams})`.
- The server also accepts `GET` with `regNo/studentId/firstName` and **no action** as `upsert` (legacy) — you do not need this.

**Response:** JSON `{status:'ok'|'error'|'notfound', message?, code?, ...data}`.
Known error codes: `auth` (session expired → auto logout with toast "🔒 Session संपले — कृपया पुन्हा Login करा."), `badcred`, `locked` (8 wrong attempts → 15 min), `badrole`, `forbidden`, `runlost`, `relogin`.

**Auth:**
- `action=login&username=..&password=..` (public) → `{status:'ok', token, exp, user:{username, role, label, assignedClass}}`. Token is HMAC signed, **12 hours** TTL. Public actions without token: `ping`, `login`, `verify`.
- Attach `token` to every other request. The token carries the role and (for teachers) the class; the server overrides class parameters for teachers — never trust UI-only filtering.
- `action=ping` → `{status:'ok', message:'Connected! Sheet: <name>', version:'V19.65', acYear:'2026-27'}`; compare `version` with the app version; show the academic-year badge from `acYear`.
- Session kept in `sessionStorage` (keys `sgs_login_user`, session key). Logout clears it.

**Roles (exact page access):**

| Role | Allowed pages (default landing page first) |
|---|---|
| `super` | dashboard, student, lc, bonafide, attendance, search, history, users, profile, stats, maintenance, classinfo, report, superadmin, attanalytics, earlyleave, scholarship, teacherlist, archive, dataqc, help |
| `master` | same as super **except** `superadmin` and `dataqc` |
| `deo` (Data Operator) | **student**, search, history, users, profile, teacherlist, help |
| `cert` | **bonafide**, attendance, search, history, users, profile, help (only certificate fields editable: bf_regNo, bf_stxt2, bf_stxt57, bf_stxt3, bf_stxt3_sel, bf_stxt6; at_regNo, at_stxt2, at_stxt57, at_stxt3, at_stxt3_sel, at_stxt16, at_stxt17, at_stxt5, at_stxt6, at_stxt14) |
| `teacher` (वर्ग शिक्षक) | **teacher**, profile, report, earlyleave, scholarship, help — limited to own class (`assignedClass` = `"<इयत्ता>|<तुकडी>"`) |
| `peon` (शिपाई) | **earlyleave**, search, profile, teacherlist, help — server allows only: getAll, getEarlyLeavePeon, markEarlyLeaveOut, changePassword, getPhotoData, getClassTeachers, logClientErrors |

Body gets class `role-<role>`; elements marked `master-only`, `super-only`, `data-master-only` are hidden for other roles. Unauthorised page → redirect to the role's default page.

